===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{cx|transitive}} To [[flow]] over the [[brim]] of (a [[container]]).
#: ''The river '''overflowed''' the levee.''
# {{cx|transitive}} To cover with a liquid, literally or figuratively.
#: ''The flash flood '''overflowed''' most of the park land and some homes.''
# {{cx|transitive}} To cause an overflow. {{rfex}}
# {{cx|intransitive}} To flow over the edge of a container.
#: ''The waters '''overflowed''' into the Ninth Ward.''
# {{cx|intransitive}} To exceed limits or capacity.
#: ''The hospital ER was '''overflowing''' with flu cases.''
## {{context|computing|ambitransitive|lang=en}} To [[exceed]] the available [[numeric]] [[range]].
##: ''Calculating 255+1 will '''overflow''' an eight-bit byte.''
# {{cx|intransitive}} To be superabundant; to abound.
#: {{rfquotek|Rogers}}

